# WP26's walk, on any server that hosts on its own: two clients walk a square each and see each other where their
# own clients are. It sends only clientSnapshot, so a server's setPosition corrections in a capture are its
# rubber-bands; vanilla sends none on this script. Shard needs player units (WP23) and entity sync (WP25).
#
#   rig/run.sh --server 'tcpdump -Z root -i lo -U -s 0 -w lo.pcap tcp port 6567 & exec "$RIG"/vm/vanilla-server.sh serpulo/groundZero -- host Ground_Zero' \
#     --clients 2 --script rig/scenarios/intent-walk.rig
#   rig/run.sh --push <shard install> --server 'tcpdump -Z root -i lo -U -s 0 -w lo.pcap tcp port 6567 & exec "$RIG"/vm/shard-server.sh maze' \
#     --clients 2 --script rig/scenarios/intent-walk.rig
#   then: python3 rig/arcnet-pcap.py <run>/server/lo.pcap --show 100000 | grep -ci setposition    (the corrections)
#
# On Shard, `console input maze` after it prints what admission saw; shard-intent-walk.rig checks that.
timeout 5m

wait port 90s
alpha: join
bravo: join
all: shot joined

alpha: mark
alpha: hold D 400ms
alpha: expect moved 2
bravo: expect player alpha within 1 5s
alpha: hold W 300ms
bravo: expect player alpha within 1 5s
alpha: hold A 400ms
bravo: expect player alpha within 1 5s
alpha: hold S 300ms
bravo: expect player alpha within 1 5s

bravo: mark
bravo: hold W+D 400ms
bravo: expect moved 2
alpha: expect player bravo within 1 5s
bravo: hold S+A 400ms
alpha: expect player bravo within 1 5s
all: shot walked

# standing still: the server's position stays the client's
wait 3s
alpha: expect player bravo within 1 2s
bravo: expect player alpha within 1 2s

assert clean all
